// 1. THE CYCLE
//
// Everything in strudel is measured in cycles, not bars or beats.
// One cycle is one loop. The tempo row in the panel sets how long it lasts.
//
// A pattern is not a list of notes you step through. It is a function:
// "given a stretch of time, what happens in it?" strudel-term asks that
// question about 50 times a second, a fraction ahead of the speaker.
//
// The practical upshot: whatever is inside the quotes gets divided evenly
// across ONE cycle, however many things you put there.

sound("bd bd bd bd")
// one hit per cycle

// Try replacing the line above with each of these, one at a time:
//
//   sound("bd bd")        two hits, each half a cycle
//   sound("bd bd bd")     three hits, each a third
//   sound("bd sn")        two different sounds
//   sound("bd sn hh cp")  four
//
// Notice you never wrote a duration. You said what goes in the cycle and
// the cycle divided itself. That is the whole trick.
